3. Notification Bug Fix: NotificationWriterService.java
[cite_start]The reason notifications were not being delivered during async processing is that Propagation.MANDATORY requires an active transaction on the current thread. Since @Async methods run on a separate thread pool (bulkExecutor), they do not inherit the transaction from the controller.
Updated Code:
/**
 * Rule 3: This service uses REQUIRES_NEW to fix the "Async Notification Bug".
 * Because batch creation happens in a background @Async thread, Propagation.MANDATORY 
 * would fail as there is no transaction bound to the new thread. 
 * REQUIRES_NEW ensures the notification is saved even if the main thread 
 * hasn't committed yet.
 */
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class NotificationWriterService {

    private final NotificationRepository notificationRepository;

